Why Is Demand Increasing
Stricter Emission Regulations: IMO 2020 and MARPOL Annex VI requirements are encouraging ship operators to adopt exhaust gas cleaning technologies to reduce sulfur emissions.
Cost-Effective Compliance: Scrubber systems provide ship operators with an alternative compliance pathway compared with switching entirely to low-sulfur fuels, particularly for high-fuel-consumption vessels.
Fleet Modernization: Retrofitting existing vessels and upgrading maritime fleets are supporting demand for open-loop, closed-loop, and hybrid scrubber systems.

Marine Exhaust Scrubber Watch: Hybrid Technology
Hybrid scrubbers are gaining strong market attention because they can operate in both open-loop and closed-loop modes. This flexibility helps vessels adapt to different regulatory environments and operating conditions. Manufacturers are also developing compact systems, improved water-treatment technologies, predictive monitoring, and advanced filtration solutions to improve performance and reduce maintenance requirements.

